{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Who say, etc.</b> It is possible that ימהר is a transitive verb, like וימהרו את המן (Esther 5:5). And it is possible that יחישה alone is intransitive, and both came as futures without a conjunction (בלא דבק), like it: אל תרבו תדברו (Exodus 1:2–3). And the meaning is: Who would that these things to come would arrive, and we will see whether they are truth:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:29.618950095Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}